ite up an outline for the travel series."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le10ob07aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "series"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a number of things or events that are arranged or happen one after the other"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She had a plan for a travel series for the newspaper."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le10ob07aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "revision"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a change or a set of changes that corrects or improves something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She worked on writing her revisions for her editor."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le10ob07aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Present Perfect Tense vs. The Simple Past Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you talk about an action or an event that occurred in the past, but you do not specify when it occurred (maybe it's not relevant to say when it happened), you use the <span class=\"strong\">PRESENT PERFECT</span>. </br>When you want to say when an action or an event occurred at a specific time in the past, you use the <span class=\"strong\">SIMPLE PAST</span>.  </br>We have some time expressions for <span class=\"strong\">PRESENT PERFECT</span> which refers to indefinite time and some for <span class=\"strong\">SIMPLE PAST</span> which refers to definite time."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"PRESENT PERFECT \u2013 indefinite   \\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have done</span> it\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"for a long time</br>lately</br>since this morning</br>before</br>recently\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"PAST SIMPLE -definite\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I did it\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"yesterday.</br>last night.</br>three days ago.</br>at 8:30 p.m.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I have read that book before."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I ate chicken for dinner last night."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Had better</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Ought to</span> for What is Advisable"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the modal <span class=\"italic\">had better</span> and <span class=\"italic\">ought to</span> to give advice. You can also use <span class=\"italic\">had better</span> to express a strong suggestion.<br>You can use the contraction <span class=\"italic\">\u201c\u2018d better\u201d</span> when you speak."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Ought to</span> is express a strong request or advice.<br><span class=\"italic\">You ought to write about those experiences in our travel section.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Might want to</span> is used to express a recommendation.<br><span class=\"italic\">You might want to make some changes to your article.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Had better</span> can be used as a strong recommendation, or warning.<br><span class=\"italic\">You'd better go and make those revisions.</span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a review of 4 sentences for a restaurant in your city that you really did not like. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Wri